# DEFECT D-2: LUT images whose tile grid is wider than tall (4096x64, 2048x128, 1024x256) make the tile row index
# (z / macro_height) * 64 run past the last image row: the reference reads beyond the pixel buffer. The fake image
# buffer ends at a PROT_NONE page, so the reference crashes. A conforming implementation MUST NOT read out of
# bounds (spec S-028 D-2 states the required behaviour: reject the image, no texture, filter skipped).
source T 1920 1080 1920 1080 SRGB video
source P 1920 1080 1920 1080 SRGB video
image lut4096x64.png 4096 64 RGBA 1 0
image lut2048x128.png 2048 128 RGBA 1 0
image lut1024x256.png 1024 256 RGBA 1 0
data d1
dset d1 image_path str lut4096x64.png
filter a clut_filter 0 d1 T P
data d2
dset d2 image_path str lut2048x128.png
filter b clut_filter 0 d2 T P
data d3
dset d3 image_path str lut1024x256.png
filter c clut_filter 0 d3 T P
try tick a 0.016
try tick b 0.016
try tick c 0.016
